# Dexcom Share credentials for the DexcomG7 Omarchy plugin.
#
# Copy this file somewhere like ~/.config/omarchy-dexcom/credentials.env,
# fill in real values, then `chmod 600` it. Never commit a filled-in copy
# or paste it anywhere - treat it like any other password file.
#
# Hard-won notes from getting this working (see also the README's
# Troubleshooting section):
#
# - This MUST be the actual sensor wearer's own Dexcom G7 app login (the
#   account with Share turned on in that app's own Settings) - not a
#   separate Follow-app/follower account, and not a Caregiver account
#   watching a Dependent profile. Both of those authenticate fine but
#   return an empty glucose-values list (HTTP 200, body "[]"), because the
#   Share API only ever serves the authenticated account's own sensor.
#
# - A phone number with a "+" country code prefix (e.g. +15551234567)
#   works fine as DEXCOM_USERNAME if that's what your account's Dexcom
#   "Username" is under Manage Personal Information. This used to be
#   broken against this API but Dexcom fixed it server-side.
#
# - If login starts failing with a password you're sure is correct, do NOT
#   just retry repeatedly - Dexcom applies rate-limiting/lockout after
#   several failed attempts in a row, and the failure mode is inconsistent
#   (a 500 "AccountPasswordInvalid" fault one time, a silent all-zero-GUID
#   "success" the next). First confirm the password still works by logging
#   into the Dexcom app or myaccount.dexcom.com directly, THEN retry here.
#
# - A wrong/mismatched Dexcom "application ID" for the region (US vs OUS vs
#   Japan) or the older single-step login endpoint will also look exactly
#   like a bad password. The bundled script already uses the correct
#   region-matched ID and the current two-step
#   AuthenticatePublisherAccount -> LoginPublisherAccountById flow - if a
#   fork of this regresses that, this exact symptom is why.

DEXCOM_USERNAME=you@example.com
DEXCOM_PASSWORD=your-dexcom-password
